1
00:00:01,100 --> 00:00:03,119
[Leo] Ninety seconds for a whole program?

2
00:00:03,139 --> 00:00:05,922
[Leo] I've had meetings take longer to find the dial-in.

3
00:00:05,942 --> 00:00:07,092
[Ava] Then let's beat them.

4
00:00:07,112 --> 00:00:08,766
[Ava] Chip's got the stopwatch.

5
00:00:09,416 --> 00:00:11,516
[Ava] Over twelve months, we document,

6
00:00:11,536 --> 00:00:16,062
[Ava] approve and launch every HR policy, process and legal obligation.

7
00:00:16,082 --> 00:00:17,975
[Leo] Across 13 jurisdictions?

8
00:00:17,995 --> 00:00:20,079
[Leo] That's 438 items.

9
00:00:20,099 --> 00:00:23,384
[Leo] And we tracked them in a spreadsheet called final_v7?

10
00:00:23,404 --> 00:00:25,025
[Ava] Which is exactly the problem.

11
00:00:25,045 --> 00:00:29,100
[Ava] For a public company, every gap is audit or legal exposure.

12
00:00:29,750 --> 00:00:31,495
[Ava] Mobilize starts October 12:

13
00:00:31,515 --> 00:00:35,461
[Ava] four weeks to set up the team, tools and approval chains.

14
00:00:35,481 --> 00:00:36,566
[Leo] Then the waves.

15
00:00:36,586 --> 00:00:38,724
[Leo] Let me guess, scariest stuff first?

16
00:00:38,744 --> 00:00:39,305
[Ava] Yep.

17
00:00:39,325 --> 00:00:41,862
[Ava] Wave 1 tackles the riskiest must-haves,

18
00:00:41,882 --> 00:00:46,560
[Ava] Waves 2 and 3 finish every required item, and Wave 4 makes it stick.

19
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:49,333
[Leo] Done by October 8, 2027.

20
00:00:49,353 --> 00:00:51,215
[Leo] Blocking my calendar now.

21
00:00:51,865 --> 00:00:53,172
[Leo] Who's doing all this?

22
00:00:53,192 --> 00:00:54,591
[Leo] Please don't say me.

23
00:00:54,611 --> 00:00:57,023
[Ava] Six workstreams, each with a named lead.

24
00:00:57,043 --> 00:01:00,876
[Ava] Regional and country HR leads handle the local details.

25
00:01:00,896 --> 00:01:04,535
[Leo] Good, because Germany doesn't exactly run like Texas.

26
00:01:05,185 --> 00:01:08,563
[Ava] Every item moves through five stages: discover what exists,

27
00:01:08,583 --> 00:01:11,049
[Ava] then draft it in the standard template.

28
00:01:11,069 --> 00:01:14,911
[Leo] Then review and approve, where my emails usually go to die.

29
00:01:14,931 --> 00:01:15,649
[Ava] Not here.

30
00:01:15,669 --> 00:01:17,265
[Ava] Approvals run in the Atlas.

31
00:01:17,285 --> 00:01:20,842
[Ava] Go live means published, communicated and evidence filed.

32
00:01:21,492 --> 00:01:22,366
[Leo] Last thing.

33
00:01:22,386 --> 00:01:23,985
[Leo] Where do I find my stuff?

34
00:01:24,005 --> 00:01:25,837
[Ava] Project HQ for the big picture,

35
00:01:25,857 --> 00:01:30,089
[Ava] the Master checklist for your items, and Approvals for sign-offs.

36
00:01:30,739 --> 00:01:36,474
[Ava] That's Atlas: 438 items, five stages, four waves, one place to track them.

37
00:01:36,494 --> 00:01:38,307
[Leo] Ninety seconds, give or take.

38
00:01:38,327 --> 00:01:41,459
[Leo] Next time, we find and update your items.
